To clearly elucidate the significant differences in the luminescence of $\mathbf{1}\cdot\mathrm{CH}_{2}\mathrm{Cl}_{2}$ , $\mathbf{1}{\cdot}\mathrm{CHCl}_{3}$ and $\mathbf{1\cdotCCl_{4}}$ , DFT calculations (Figures S1-S3) were performed. We first evaluated the binding energy between the MOF and adsorbent molecules. The model used for this purpose schematically illustrated in Figure S24. State $i$ is the initial state before binding, whereas State $f$ is the final state in which adsorbent molecules of $\mathrm{CH}_{2}\mathrm{Cl}_{2}$ , $\mathrm{CHCl}_{3}$ or $\mathrm{CCl}_{4}$ are included in the MOF. It should be noted that in State $i_{;}$ the solvent molecules do not mutually interact.
