Reversibility of the Luminescence of 1. Considering the crucial importance of sensitivity, recyclability and long-term stability of sensors,23 we investigated these three factors with 1 using $\mathrm{CH}_{2}\mathrm{Cl}_{2}$ as a model. $\mathrm{CH}_{2}\mathrm{Cl}_{2}$ led to an enhancement of the luminescence intensity ca. 18-fold relative to air (off state), and the QY of $\mathbf{1}\cdot\mathrm{CH}_{2}\mathrm{Cl}_{2}$ reached up to $23.3\%$ .
A prototype sensor setup was used to test the response rate of 1 (Figure S27).9b The sensor slide was prepared by attaching 1 on a glass slide with double-sided tape. The sensor slide was exposed to pure air with or without $\mathrm{CH}_{2}\mathrm{Cl}_{2}$ vapor, in an alternating manner. The luminescence intensity at $580\ \mathrm{nm}$ was monitored continuously under excitation at $470~\mathrm{nm}$ and plotted versus time (Figure 4). Rapid writing/erasing was achieved and the light-up fluorescent response time to $\mathrm{CH}_{2}\mathrm{Cl}_{2}$ was less than $\mathrm{~\bf~l~s~}_{\mathrm{{\scriptsize~\cdot~}}}$ , limited only by the measurement apparatus. The luminescent transient response curves of 1 at room temperature for 20 cycles were recorded without noticeable performance loss, which represents an ultrafast visual light-up response compared with other vapor sensors (Figure S28).23b The real-time light-up response of 1 can be attributed to its highly permeable channels and specific weak interactions with $\mathrm{CH}_{2}\mathrm{Cl}_{2}$ , allowing easy reversibility. These features allowed $\mathrm{CH}_{2}\mathrm{Cl}_{2}$ to access the framework and lock the vibrations of the pyridyl rings to decrease the non-radiative-decay.
Traditional light-up luminescent sensors are extremely sensitive to moisture and easily lose their activity under ambient conditions,9b while complex 1 shows remarkably stable fluorescence performance (Figure 4d). This was shown by measuring the luminescence intensity under $\mathrm{CH}_{2}\mathrm{Cl}_{2}$ vapor and the response time over two weeks. The robustness of the sensor was further confirmed by its retained crystallinity after recycling, as evidenced by PXRD which established the purity and stability of the sample (Figure 4e).
